            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lucky Noodles"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Hubby is eating these straight out of the fridge! We have had them on grilled salmon and burgers and will have them on hot dogs and sandwiches too! We both prefer paper thin rings instead of chopping the onion. There may be a mistake on the recipe, way too much salt and way too little sugar. I ended up with 1/2 teaspoon salt and 4 Tablespoons sugar. And DH is eating them straight from the fridge! I said that again. . . Thank you Bobi"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DCNBLUZ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "OK, so I doubled the recipe so my amounts will reflect that. Love this recipe super easy. I made the following changes: six whole cloves of garlic, about 18 peppercorns and the same Number of allspice berries (I was shooting for three of each in the half pint jars I was making). I do a lot of canning and wasn’t sure if I was going to process this in a hot bath or not but just to be on the safe side I added the appropriate amount of pickle crisp from ball products. These turned out wonderfully and I’m asked my friends and family to make them some next time I’m buying red onions in bulk.",
            "datePublished": "2020-07-04T01:15:40.120Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Starfish"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really liked these, but next time I'll make a few changes. I would add less salt and a bit more sugar, maybe two tablespoons. Also, I tried these without steeping first and then after they'd steeped...I would skip it if you enjoy a crisper onion. They were tasty and I plan to refrigerate them until burger-nite in a few days. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-04T08:12:36.933Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Richard"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I think the recipe has a typo for the salt. It probably should be teaspoons instead of tablespoons. It was VERY salty when I used 1 1/2 Tablespoons of salt. When I doubled the other ingredients of the pickling liquid it was much better.",
            "datePublished": "2026-08-17T20:31:13.504Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ejmquilts"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are great, but I prefer them with a few changes. I cut the onion into slivers about 1 inch long. Use 1-1/2 tsp salt, not tablespoons and replace red wine vinegar with white wine vinegar.",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-06T12:19:49.397Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Strokemom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I sliced my onions not chopped. I dissolved Kosher salt and sugar in the vinegar then added the onions and stored in the fridge. I stirred them 3 times a day. I love pickled onions.",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-08T21:52:37.553Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bill Harkins"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used one red onion cut in half and sliced. Used a bottle of red wine vinegar and approximated other ingredients. Added red pepper flakes and tarragon and garlic. Didn’t boil it. Stuck it in a used mayonnaise jar and left it in the refrigerator over night. Turned out fine.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-20T17:35:44.663Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious with changes in ingredients. 1/2 tbs salt, 3 tbs sugar, 1/4 cup red wine vinegar, 1/4 cup apple cider vinegar",
            "datePublished": "2018-01-18T06:15:19.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Squankdog"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These pickled onions are a great complement to fish, sandwiches, burgers and more. Tangy, sweet and delicious. After making the recipe as written several times, I have settled on switching the amounts of sugar and salt. This quick recipe invites tweaking, so by all means use less salt and/or, more sugar to suit your taste!",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-17T19:45:09.527Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "princessgertie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were fantastic on the street tacos that I made this weekend. The only changes that I made were: 1. I split the 1/2 cup of red wine vinegar up and used 1/4 cup of red wine vinegar and 1/4 cup of apple cider vinegar, and 2. I increased the sugar to 1 tablespoon. With both of these changes, they were absolutely perfect. My friends and family were eating the onions by themselves and trying to come up with ideas of other foods that they could put them on.",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-24T17:59:53.217Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "The Robinson Family"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy and delicious. But... a bit salty for my taste. On my second round I cut the salt to 2/3 tbsp and doubled the sugar. Perfect!",
